 {"ira-the-mage-3\n10 nautical miles to the west is Snow Mountain Island.","向西10海里为雪山岛。"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA big wave hits and the water rushes to the deck.","一个大浪打来，水冲到了甲板上。"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA burly uncle looked at Ina and the others in surprise.\n{Uncle:} You rushed over my dead wood formation. Looks like you are not from Longyashan heroes, right? Scared me.\n{Ina:} We are not. By the way, uncle, you are so powerful, you can set up such a strong formation.\n{Uncle:} Ha ha, my name is Aaron, I am a craftsman and have always lived here. As a group of thieves named Longyashan heroes took control of this area recently, I had to make this deadwood formation to defend, so that they could not get through. Alas, these guys are doing evil, and the government doesn't care. If this goes on, even if I can prevent them from coming in, I won't be able to continue doing business here. I am considering moving to another place.\n{Ina:} We are planning to fight against Long Ya Shan heroes. It's just that the mountain road in front is getting steeper and steeper, I don't know if I can go up the mountain.\n{Aron:} Really? It's great that you go to crusade them. Mountain roads are not easy to climb, so I can help. I will make a kind of {\"Mountain Climbing Bike\"}, and you can easily get on it with a mountain bike. It's just that a lot of good {wood} is needed to make a mountain bike. The rotten wood around here is no good, it will break, and people will die. If you can get wood, I will make it for you.\n{Ina:} Thank you so much, uncle.\n{Aron:} You are welcome, since I have encountered a warrior who is willing to fight against thieves, I will try my best to move away later.\n{Ina:} But where does the uncle want to move?\n{Aron:} I heard that there is a very popular prince in the Koz Peninsula to the north of Kartia, ruling the place. The people live and work in peace and contentment. There is no bandit or harsh government. It sounds really tempting, so I plan to go there. . How could there not be such a place in Barland?\n{Ina:} Ah, this is not...\n{Freeman:} (Shh~~~~~~)\n{Ina:} (Jack is really amazing, and his popularity has spread to foreign countries.)","一个身材魁梧的大叔吃惊地望着伊娜他们。\n\n{大叔：}我的枯木阵竟然被你们闯过来了。看上去你们不是龙牙山好汉一伙的吧？吓死我了。\n{伊娜：}我们不是啦。话说大叔你好厉害，能布下这么强的阵。\n{大叔：}呵呵，我叫阿隆，是个工匠，一直住在这里。由于近段时间有一伙叫龙牙山好汉的盗贼控制了这一带，我不得不制作了这个枯木阵进行防卫，这样他们就过不来了。唉，这群家伙为非作歹，政府也不管，这样下去，就算我能阻止他们进来，也没法继续在这里做生意了。我正考虑搬迁到别的地方去呢。\n{伊娜：}我们正打算去讨伐龙牙山好汉呢。只是前面的山路越来越陡，不知道是不是能上得了山去。\n{阿隆：}是吗？你们去讨伐他们，太好了。山路不好攀登，这个我能帮忙。我会制作一种{“攀山车”}，用了攀山车，你们就能很容易登上去了。只是制作攀山车需要不少上好的{木材}，这里周围的烂木头可不行，会断的，要摔死人。如果你们能弄到木材的话，我就给你们制作。\n{伊娜：}太谢谢大叔了。\n{阿隆：}不用客气，既然遇到了肯讨伐盗贼的勇士，我就尽点力，迟点再搬走好了。\n{伊娜：}不过大叔想搬去哪里呢？\n{阿隆：}我听说卡尔提亚北面的科兹半岛，有一个很得人心的王子治理着那块地方，百姓安居乐业，既无盗匪也无苛政，听上去真是诱人，所以我打算去那里。巴兰德怎么就没有这样的地方呢。\n{伊娜：}啊，这不是……\n{弗里曼：}（嘘~~~~~~）\n{伊娜：}（杰克真了不起，人气都传到外国了。）"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA dark manhole cover was abandoned in the corner.\n{Ina:} Hey, why is there a shady manhole cover here?\n{Freeman:} Maybe someone stole it and dropped it here.\n{Ina:} Steal the yin manhole cover too? This would be very dangerous. If others accidentally fall into the well...\n{Freeman:} Well, some people are so poor that they will get the idea of the well cover. Although they can't sell for a few dollars, It's easy to steal, and at least you can have another meal after stealing it. This phenomenon is especially common when the country practices harsh government like Archbishop Yingluck.\n{Ina:} It seems that we must stop Archbishop Yingluck as soon as possible... so that everyone can live a stable life and eat.\n{Freeman:} I think so too, so now we will stand on the same front.\n{Ina:} However, it is a pity that this shady manhole cover is abandoned here, let me put it away first.","一个阴井盖被遗弃在角落里。\n\n{伊娜：}咦，这里怎么会有个阴井盖啊？\n{弗里曼：}可能是谁偷来了掉落在这里的吧。\n{伊娜：}阴井盖也要偷？这样会很危险啊，如果别人不小心掉进了阴井……\n{弗里曼：}嗯，有些人实在穷得没办法了，就会打上阴井盖的主意，虽然卖不了几个钱，但是偷起来方便，偷了之后至少也能换一顿饭吃。当国家实行英拉大主教那样的苛政时，这种现象就尤其多。\n{伊娜：}看来我们必须尽快阻止英拉大主教才行……要让大家都能安定生活有饭吃。\n{弗里曼：}我也是这么想的，所以现在我们才会站到同一个阵线上。\n{伊娜：}不过，这个阴井盖遗弃在这里太可惜了，我先把它收起来吧。\n\n\n"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA delicate fish-shaped necklace.","一条精致的鱼形项链。"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA demon who looked like a small leader was searching for something.\n{Ina:} Excuse me...\n{Demon Captain:} What? Humanity? The Demon Captain drew out the knife, but after thinking about it, he took it back. {Captain of the Demon Race:} Humans, come here, I want to ask you a question.\n{Ina:} It just so happens that I also want to ask you a question. This was originally the territory of the Kingdom of Trifia, why did you come here, and how can it be so messed up here that the residents can't see it?\n{Captain Demon:} Hahaha, I thought it was something wrong. The Trifiya Kingdom has been occupied by our demons. I heard that the demons of the Aryanian continent unified the continent under the leadership of the dark prince Pallas. Why are the demons of Mirronia willing to fall behind? Now we are also helped by the nobles. It is only time to conquer the human ruled area. problem.\n{Rael:} What's going on here, who do you mean by \"noble people helping each other\"? {Captain of the Demon Race:} You don't need to know this anymore. Let me ask. Do you know where {\"Dragonbone Greaves\"} is located? Or have you ever seen a pair of bone guards?\n{Ina:} Ah! {Rael:} (Calm down, don't let him see it.)\n{Ina:} I haven't seen this thing. {Captain of the Demon Race:} Really, since I haven't seen it, then you are of no use to me, I will send you to hell, hahaha!","一个看似小头领的魔族正在搜查着什么。\n\n{伊娜：}打扰一下……\n{魔族队长：}什么？人类？\n\n魔族队长拔出刀，但考虑了一下，又收了回去。\n\n{魔族队长：}人类，你们过来，我想问你们个问题。\n{伊娜：}正巧，我也想问你个问题。这里本来是特里菲亚王国的领土，你们怎么会跑到这里来，而这里又怎么会到处乱七八糟连居民都看不到？\n{魔族队长：}哈哈哈，我还以为是什么问题。特里菲亚王国已经被我们魔族占领了。听说亚利安尼亚大陆的魔族在暗黑王子帕拉斯的领导下统一了大陆，我们米尔罗尼亚的魔族怎么甘心落后呢，现在我们也得到了贵人相助，征服人类统治区只是时间问题。\n{雷尔：}这是怎么回事，你所谓的“贵人相助”又是指的谁？\n{魔族队长：}这个你们没有必要知道了。下面换我问了。你们知不知道{“龙骨胫甲”}在什么地方？或者有没有见过一对骨头做成的护腿？\n{伊娜：}啊！\n{雷尔：}（镇静，别让他看出来。）\n{伊娜：}没见过这个东西耶。\n{魔族队长：}是吗，既然没见过，那么你们就对我没有用处了，我这就送你们下地狱，啊哈哈哈！"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA dwarf is tied to the rock pillar in front. Seeing Ina and others approaching, she hurriedly called for help.\n{Ina:} Ah, this is not... Mr. Bad Guy!\n{Da Wu:} It's actually you, stupid girl, quickly help this lord to untie the rope.\n{Ina:} Why should I help you untie? You always scold me for a stupid little girl, and every time you blackmail money.\n{Da Wu:} Don't say that is good, this lord has also been called Mr. Bad Guy by you, this is even. As for the money collected, it is all the information fee of the adult in exchange for the blood and sweat-otherwise, if you save the adult, the adult will answer your question for free. Is this good?\n{Ina:} Cut, who cares about your answer.\n{Dawu:} Alright, let's do it, this lord makes an exception to give you a special discount and answer two questions for free, okay?\n{Ina:} Okay, well, don't bargain with me. I will save you.\n{Ina:} Speaking of which, Mr. Bad, why are you tied up here? Aren't you very magical?\n{Da Wu:} Hey, it is precisely because of the great supernatural powers of this lord that he was only tied up here. After you changed your stupid little girl, most of them were dead. When my lord passed by here today, he happened to see two demons sneaking in here, and he secretly took a look. As a result, it was only because of a moment of confusion and negligence that the wise man must have lost his mind. When they found out, they caught Ben. Originally, they wanted to kill this lord and kill him. Then, when this lord's cleverness and cleverness came to mind, they said to them, \"This lord knows where what you are looking for\", they did not kill this lord.\n{Ina:} Then do you really know where they are looking for?\n{Dawu:} Of course I know. It's just that the lord won't just say it so simply. You know, once you make it clear, they will definitely kill the lord, so the lord just vaguely told them to go west and look for it. Then they tied this lord here and looked for it themselves.\n{Ina:} If the information you give is wrong, they will still come back and kill you.\n{Da Wu:} Hey, how could it be wrong? It must be in the west, you stupid little girl. Because there is no road to the east.\n{Ina:} So where is the specific location of what they are looking for?\n{Dawu:} Well, the information fee is 3000 gold coins.\n{Ina:} Didn't you say it's free?\n{Da Wu:} My lord said to answer two questions for free. You are already the third one. Of course you will have to charge. The first question is \"Why are people tied here\", and the second is \"Do you really know where what they are looking for\".\n{Ina:} This is also a problem, you are too treacherous. Forget it, I won't ask you anymore. Actually, I tell you, what they are looking for is in my hands. I just pretended to ask you just to see if you really knew it. Since you don't know, I don't need to ask you again.\n{Da Wu:} Oh, don't do this. It's not easy for this adult to live a life, so I just beg for food for selling some information. Well, this lord will teach you how to crack the mechanism that I just stole from the two demons, and use this to exchange 3000 gold coins for the information fee, isn't it too much? If you don't have this, you will be easily trapped in this area, and there will be great dangers.\n{Ina:} Should I believe you?\n{Dawu:} When did the lord fool you. Think about it for yourself. When did the help provided by this adult not be genuine?\n{Ina:} That's also true... well, since you haven't lied to me before, just trust you again.","前面的岩石柱上绑着一个矮子。看到伊娜等人走近，连忙大声呼救。\n\n{伊娜：}啊，这不是……坏人先生！\n{达伍：}居然是你，笨小丫头，快帮本大人解开绳子。\n{伊娜：}我为什么要帮你解开啊，你每次都骂我笨小丫头，还每次敲诈钱财。\n{达伍：}不要说那些好啦，本大人不是也被你叫成坏人先生了嘛，这就扯平了。至于收的钱，那都是本大人血汗换来的信息费啊——要不这样吧，你救本大人下来，本大人就免费回答你一个问题。这样好不好？\n{伊娜：}切，谁稀罕你的回答。\n{达伍：}行行好啦，这样吧，本大人破例给你来个特大优惠，免费回答两个问题，好不好？\n{伊娜：}好了好了别跟我讨价还价了。我救你就是了。\n{伊娜：}说起来，坏人先生，你怎么会被人绑在这里啊？你不是很神通广大的吗？\n{达伍：}嘿嘿，正是因为本大人神通广大，才只是被绑在这里，换了你这笨小丫头，多半已经没命了。本大人今天路过这里时，正巧看到两个魔族的人在这里鬼鬼祟祟地布置什么机关，就偷偷地看了。结果只因一时糊涂疏忽大意智者千虑必有一失，被他们发现了，他们就把本大人抓住了。本来他们就想杀了本大人灭口，然后本大人神机妙算灵机一动急中生智计上心头，就对他们说，“本大人知道你们要找的东西在哪里”，他们就没杀本大人。\n{伊娜：}那么你真知道他们要找的东西在哪里吗？\n{达伍：}本大人当然知道。只是本大人不会就这么简单说出来，要知道，一旦说清楚了，他们一定会杀了本大人，所以本大人只是模糊地告诉他们往西边走去找找。然后他们就把本大人绑在这里，自己去找了。\n{伊娜：}如果你给的信息是错的，他们还是会回来杀了你。\n{达伍：}嘿嘿，怎么可能是错的，肯定在西边啦，你这笨小丫头。因为东边没路了嘛。\n{伊娜：}那么他们要找的东西的具体位置在哪里呢？\n{达伍：}这个嘛，信息费3000金币。\n{伊娜：}你不是说免费嘛？\n{达伍：}本大人说了免费回答两个问题啊，你这已经是第三个了，当然要收费了。第一个问题是“为什么被人绑在这里”，第二个是“你真的知道他们要找的东西在哪里吗”。\n{伊娜：}这也算问题啊，你太奸诈了。算了，我不问你了。其实啊，我告诉你，他们要找的东西就在我手上，我就是想看看你是不是真知道，才假装问你的。既然你不知道，我也没必要再问你了。\n{达伍：}唉，不要这样嘛，本大人生活也不容易，也就为了卖点信息费讨口饭吃。这样吧，本大人把刚刚从那两个魔族那里偷学来的机关破解法教给你，拿这个换3000金币信息费，不过分吧？要是没有这个，你们在这一带很容易中陷阱，会有巨大的危险哦。\n{伊娜：}我应该相信你吗？\n{达伍：}本大人什么时候骗过你了。你自己想想，本大人给你提供的帮助，哪次不是货真价实？\n{伊娜：}这么说也是……好吧，看在你以前没骗过我的份上，就再相信你一次好了。\n\n\n\n"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA few puppies shrank tiredly in the corner of the cave.\n{Ina:} Where is your mother? It's so pitiful, is it abandoned? I will take you away.","岩洞的一角倦缩着几只小狗崽。\n\n{伊娜：}你们的妈妈呢？真可怜，难道是被遗弃了？我带你们走吧。"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA firebird flew out of a crack in the ice rock.\n{Firebird:} Haha, finally free! what? Humanity? kill!","冰岩的裂缝中突然飞出一只火鸟。\n\n{火鸟：}哈哈，终于自由了！什么？人类？杀！"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA gray stone storefront that is not too spacious is hung with a wooden sign with a picture of a four-legged cup. It looks like a pub. There were five or six guests sitting sporadically inside.\n{Waiter:} The customer would like to ask, what would you like to drink? This is our menu.\n{Rael:} Ina, you point, madam first.\n{Ina:} Ah, let me see... what are these? The blood of Qisi, Delal's white slime, Delal's green slime, blue wine...\n{Waiter:} Looks like you are humans. Then I recommend you this, wolf eye juice, which is relatively light, and it is generally suitable for those who are not used to the heavy taste.\n{Ina:} Uh, I don't know what it is, but since you recommend it so, let's do it. Rael, Jack, how about you?\n{Rael:} It's just as good.\n{Freeman:} Me too.\n{Waiter:} Good. Three wolf eye juices, 600 gold coins.\n{Ina:} So expensive. I remember that a glass of wine in my pub over there was only 30 gold coins.\n{Freeman:} Even Kartia is no more than 50 gold coins. However, the prices here seem to be very different.\n{Ina:} Isn't it because we are human beings deliberately slaughter us?\n{Freeman:} I think it is more likely to be caused by different labor costs. Because of the ever-expanding population of human beings, labor costs are getting lower and lower, and prices are lower. I really don't know what's going on in the Demon World, but it may be better controlled than humans.\n{Ina:} Jack is so good, I know everything...\n{Freeman:} I went to economics class, but this is just a guess. We have to find local people to understand it clearly before we know.\n{Ina:} Look at the person on the table next to him. It seems that he is also a human. Let's ask?","一家灰石砌成的不算太宽敞的店面，挂着一块画着四脚杯的木牌。看上去是个酒馆。里面零星地坐着五六个客人。\n\n{服务员：}客倌有请，要喝点什么？这是我们的菜单。\n{雷尔：}伊娜，你点，女士优先。\n{伊娜：}啊，那我来看看……这些都是什么呀？奇丝之血，德拉尔白粘液，德拉尔绿粘液，蓝腥酒……\n{服务员：}看起来你们是人类吧。那还是推荐你们这个，狼眼果汁，比较清淡的，吃不惯重口味的一般会适宜这个。\n{伊娜：}呃，虽然不知道是什么东西，不过既然你这么推荐了，就要这个吧。雷尔，杰克，你们呢？\n{雷尔：}一样好了。\n{弗里曼：}我也是。\n{服务员：}好。三份狼眼果汁，600金币。\n{伊娜：}好贵啊。我记得我家那边的酒馆一杯酒不过30金币的嘛。\n{弗里曼：}即使是卡尔提亚也不过50金币。不过，这里的物价看来很不同。\n{伊娜：}不会是看我们是人类故意宰我们吧？\n{弗里曼：}我觉得更可能是劳动力成本不同导致的吧。人类因为一直不断膨胀的人口，劳动力成本越来越低，物价就低。魔界这边是怎么样个情况我还真不了解，不过可能控制得比人类好。\n{伊娜：}杰克好厉害，这都知道……\n{弗里曼：}经济课上学的，不过这也只是猜测而已。我们得找当地人了解清楚才知道。\n{伊娜：}你看旁边桌上那位，好像也是人类耶，我们去问问？\n\n\n\n"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA group of archers gathered here.\n{Ina:} What are you doing here?\n{Sagittarius:} Hey, was it discovered by you? We thought we were quite hidden. Okay, since you found us, why don't you come and do us a favor?\n{Ina:} What's the matter?\n{Archer:} We are practicing archery. It's just that Zheng Chou has no suitable target. With an apple on your head, stand in front and let us practice shooting that apple. How about?\n{Ina:} Hey, this is too dangerous, right?\n{Sagittarius:} If you agree, we will give you a medal as a reward. Of course, there is one thing to say before, if you are shot to death by us, we are not responsible either.\n{Ina:} This...I think about it.","一群射手在这里聚集着。\n{伊娜：}你们在这里干什么呢？\n{射手：}咦，被你发现啦？我们还以为我们藏得挺隐蔽的了。也好，既然你发现了我们，不如来帮我们一个忙怎么样？\n{伊娜：}什么事呢？\n{射手：}我们正在练习箭法呢。只是正愁没有合适的靶子。你头顶一个苹果，站到前面去，让我们练习射那个苹果，怎么样？\n{伊娜：}喂，这也太危险了吧？\n{射手：}你要是答应了，我们就给你一个勋章作为奖励。当然，有一句话要说在前头，如果你被我们射死了，我们也不负责任哦。\n{伊娜：}这个……我考虑考虑。\n\n"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA group of farmers gathered around the road and looked at Ina and the three of them.\n{Freeman:} Huh? What are you doing here?\n{Farmer:} Your Royal Highness, are you His Royal Highness Prince Freeman?\n{Farmer:} We have all seen just now, you knocked down General Bruno, the confidant of Archbishop Yingluck.\n{Farmer:} We will not believe the lie that Bishop Yingdara told His Royal Highness that the Prince was treasonous, we support His Highness Freeman.\n{Farmer:} Archbishop Yingluck has levied too much tax on us. If we don't pay, we will be arrested and put into hard labor. We are exploited to nothing! Please lead us against the tyranny of Archbishop Yingluck!\n{Freeman:} Thank you everyone, with your support, I am more confident. I am here because I want to fight against Archbishop Yingluck and rebuild the peaceful and prosperous Kingdom of Kartia. Everyone is living too poorly. Let me support you 10,000 gold coins first. Although the number is not large, I hope to help you tide over the difficulties and usher in a good harvest.\n{Farmer:} Great, the place where His Royal Highness is useful to us, {Go through fire and water without any hesitation}. We have had enough of the oppression of Archbishop Yingluck and General Bruno, we have to follow His Royal Highness Prince Freeman to create a new country!","一群农民围在路边看着伊娜他们三人。\n\n{弗里曼：}唉？大家这是在干什么呢？\n{农民：}王子殿下，您是弗里曼王子殿下吧？\n{农民：}刚才我们都看见了，你们把布里诺将军，那个英拉大主教的亲信打倒了。\n{农民：}我们不会相信英大拉主教说王子殿下叛国的谎言，我们拥护弗里曼王子殿下。\n{农民：}英拉大主教对我们征的税太重了，不交就要被抓去做苦役，我们被剥削得什么都没有了！请王子殿下带领我们反抗英拉大主教的暴政吧！\n{弗里曼：}谢谢大家，有了大家的支持，我更有信心了。我来这里，就是想要对抗英拉大主教，重建和平富饶的卡尔提亚王国的。大家日子过得太贫苦了，我先支援你们10000金币吧，虽然数目不多，希望能帮助你们渡过难关，迎来丰收的时刻。\n{农民：}太好了，王子殿下有用得着我们的地方，{赴汤蹈火再所不辞}。英拉大主教和布里诺将军的欺压我们受够了，我们要跟着弗里曼王子殿下开创新的国家！"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA group of harpies suddenly jumped down from the air.\n{Ina:} Ah, it's here again, they are all flying, bullying us...","一群鹰身女妖突然从空中扑了下来。\n\n{伊娜：}啊，果然又来了，都是会飞的啊，欺负我们……"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA group of monsters escorted a man in sacrificial robes down the mountain. One of the monsters, who looked like a small boss, reprimanded the man viciously.\n{Monster:} You bastard, have been leading us around since just now, wanting to play us?\n{Man:} Ouch, my lord, I dare not.\n{Monster:} Give you another 10 minutes. If you still don't take us to the place where the treasure is buried, I will chop off your head!\n{Man:} My lord, 10 minutes is too little, this mountain road is not easy to walk...\n{Monster:} Let's bargain with Lao Tzu, we have been following you for a long time, and we are about to turn this mountain around. Don't think that only you know where the treasure is and you can always deceive us. Lao Tzu's patience is limited. If you have finished Lao Tzu's patience, even if you don't need the treasure, you will cut your head!\n{Man:} Well, well, don't worry, sir, we will be there soon, soon...\n{Ina:} Who are you, why are you bullying people so much? Let go of that gentleman.\n{Monster:} Huh? Humanity? There are still human beings who do not know how to live or die dare to speak to Lao Tzu. Brothers, come on, chop them off!","一群怪物押着一个身穿祭袍的男子从山上走下来。其中一个看似小头目的怪物对男子恶狠狠地训斥着。\n\n{怪物：}你这混蛋，从刚才起就一直带着我们绕圈子，想耍我们？\n{男子：}哎哟，大人，我不敢啊。\n{怪物：}再给你10分钟的时间，如果你还不把我们带到埋藏宝物的地方，老子就砍了你的脑袋！\n{男子：}大人，10分钟是不是太少了，这山路不好走……\n{怪物：}少跟老子讨价还价，我们已经跟着你转了半天了，都快把这山里转遍了。你别以为只有你知道宝物在哪就可以一直把我们骗得团团转，老子的耐心是有限度的，把老子的耐心磨完了，就算不要宝物也砍了你的脑袋！\n{男子：}这，好好，大人您别急，我们很快就会到，很快……\n\n{伊娜：}你们谁啊，怎么这么欺负人的？把那位先生放开。\n{怪物：}嗯？人类？居然还有不知死活的人类敢对老子这么说话。弟兄们，上，剁了他们！\n\n\n"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA huge animal was lying listlessly beside the oak forest. He was the size of Little Bimon, with big fan-like ears and a long nose.\n{Ina:} Hey, this animal is curious about Teye. I have never seen an animal like this. Have you seen it?\n{Rael:} I haven't seen it.\n{Freeman:} It seems that I have seen it in the book. I have an impression, let me think about it...\n{Animal:} What do you look at? Haven't seen an elephant?\n{Freeman:} That's right, it turned out to be an elephant!\n{Elephant:} Rare and weird...\n{Ina:} Mr. Elephant...\n{Elephant:}... {Ina:} Mr. Elephant, what's wrong with you, you are so insane...\n{Rael:} Eri He looks ignorant and irritable, so let's just leave him alone.\n{Ina:} But Mr. Elephant seems to be in trouble. I want to see if I can help.\n{Elephant:} I'm going to starve to death. If you are so kind, help me get some tender branches.\n{Ina:} But, isn't it all around here?\n{Elephant:} Take a look, the trees around here are called \"oak trees\". I am an \"elephant\", so how can I eat an \"oak tree\"? I grew up on the same root.\n{Ina:} Uh, this, all right. I think of a way to get some other branches.","一只巨大的动物无精打采地趴在橡树林边。他的身材有小比蒙那么大，长着一对巨扇般的大耳朵和一条长长的鼻子。\n\n{伊娜：}咦，这只动物好奇特耶。我从来没见过这种样子的动物。你们见过吗？\n{雷尔：}没见过。\n{弗里曼：}好像有在书上见到的，我点印象，让我想想……\n{动物：}看什么看，没看过大象啊？\n{弗里曼：}对啦，原来就是大象！\n{大象：}少见多怪……\n{伊娜：}大象先生……\n{大象：}……\n{伊娜：}大象先生，你怎么了，这么没精神……\n{雷尔：}爱理不理的样子，又很烦躁，我们还是不要管他好了。\n{伊娜：}可是大象先生看起来有麻烦呢，我想看看能不能帮帮忙什么的。\n{大象：}我快要饿死了啦。如果你有这好心，帮我弄点嫩树枝来吧。\n{伊娜：}可是，这周围不就都是树林吗？\n{大象：}你看看清楚，这周围的树，叫“橡树”。我是“象”，怎么能吃“橡树”呢，跟我本是同根生嘛。\n{伊娜：}呃，这个，好吧。我想办法去弄点别的树枝来。\n\n\n\n"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA man in a long robe looked like a messenger, holding the notice in one hand, and was reading it. A group of people around were watching, and some were talking about it.","一个穿着长袍的人，看上去是个差人模样，一手捧着布告，正在宣读。周围一群人在围观，有的则议论纷纷。\n"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA man in black ran in panic, and was caught by Ina and the others.\n{Freeman:} It's from the Black Tigers, the same clothes.\n{Ina:} Here are the minions of Archbishop Yingluck.\n{Rael:} Are you hiding there and wanting to plot against us?\n{Man:} Are you not with the men in black? I thought you were in their gang, and my identity was exposed, so I ran away in fright. Can you help me?\n{Ina:} What's the matter, you are not from Archbishop Yingluck?\n{Man:} My name is Sam. I was originally a resident of Bilesburg. I was arrested to do hard work to build this tower. It was the people in black clothes who looked after us. Fortunately, I was clever and stole a piece of their clothes. After finishing the construction, all the companions who were captured were killed by them. I passed the test by wearing their clothes, so I survived.\n{Rael:} Now that you have a disguise, why don't you abscond?\n{Sam:} There are corpses everywhere in the depths of this cave. I am afraid and dare not to enter. I'm worried about whether I'm going to die here. Fortunately, I met you, please, take me out...\n{Freeman:} (Should we trust him?)\n{Rael:} (It is also possible It's the Black Tiger agents who deliberately pretended to deceive us, maybe.)\n{Ina:} (But you see, this person is so pitiful, skinny, and seems to have been hungry for a long time. The subordinates of Archbishop Yingluck, one by one. They're as strong as cows, wouldn't they look like this? So I plan to believe him.)\n{Freeman:} (Yes.)\n{Ina:} Okay, then let's go with us.\n{Sam:} Thank you so much!","一个黑衣人慌慌张张地向里跑，被伊娜他们追上一把抓住。\n\n{弗里曼：}又是黑虎特工队的，一样的衣服。\n{伊娜：}这边还有英拉大主教的爪牙。\n{雷尔：}躲在那里想要暗算我们吗？\n{男子：}你们不是跟黑衣人他们一伙的？我还以为你们是他们一伙的，我的身份暴露了，才吓得拔腿就跑。你们能不能救救我？\n{伊娜：}怎么回事，你不是英拉大主教的人？\n{男子：}我叫萨姆，本来是比勒斯勃格的居民，被抓来做苦工修建这个塔，看管我们的就是穿这种黑衣服的人。我好在一时机灵，偷了一件他们的衣服。造完之后，一起被抓来的同伴都被他们杀了，我穿了他们的衣服蒙混过关，所以活了下来。\n{雷尔：}既然你有了伪装，怎么不潜逃出去呢？\n{萨姆：}这洞的深处到处是尸体，我害怕，不敢乱闯。我正担心自己是不是要死在这里面了，还好遇到了你们，求求你们，带我出去吧……\n{弗里曼：}（我们要相信他吗？）\n{雷尔：}（也有可能是黑虎特工队的人故意装的想骗我们上当也说不定。）\n{伊娜：}（可是你们看这个人好可怜，骨瘦如柴，像是饿了很久了。英拉大主教的手下， 一个个都健壮如牛，不会这个样子的吧？所以我打算相信他。）\n{弗里曼：}（也对。）\n{伊娜：}好吧，那么就跟我们一起走吧。\n{萨姆：}太感谢了！\n\n\n"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA narrow waterway meanders to the point where it is not visible.","一条狭窄的水道蜿蜒至深不可见处。"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA plaque hung on a large cave with a few large characters: \"Hailong Palace\".\n{Ina:} It seems that there is nothing wrong here.","一处宽大的洞穴上面挂着一块牌匾，上面写着几个大字：“海龙宫”。\n\n{伊娜：}看来就是这里没错了。"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA sandstorm swept across the sky.","一阵沙尘暴席天卷地而来。"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA scholar-like figure was surrounded by a group of thugs riding knives.\n{Evil:} You dead alchemist, understand if you don't pay protection fees and smash your house!\n{Scholar:} My sirs, I really don't have any money. You came here last week and took away my last savings. How can I still have money?\n{Evil:} Are you not an alchemist? Can't make gold in a week?\n{Scholar:} Alchemy is just a general term for the study of some mysterious phenomena mainly based on chemistry, not gold alchemy.\n{Evil:} I want to fool us, no way! You must hand over the money today, otherwise...\n{Ina:} Stop, don't bring such bullies.\n{Evil:} Huh? Who are you again? Are you friends of this dead alchemist? Come to pay for him?\n{Ina:} I heard it just now, why are you blackmailing others?\n{Evil:} We are the heroes of Longyashan!\n{Ina:} It's another Longyashan hero, a group of robbers.\n{Evil:} How dare you say that we are robbers, you are living impatiently! Brothers, clean up this girl first, and then deal with the dead alchemist.","一个学者模样的人被一群骑马拿刀的恶徒包围着。\n{恶徒：}你个死炼金术士，听明白没有，不交保护费，把你的房子砸烂！\n{学者：}各位大人，我实在是没有钱了。上周你们就来过了，把我最后的积蓄都拿走了，我哪还有钱啊？\n{恶徒：}你不是炼金术士吗？一周的时间还炼不出黄金？\n{学者：}炼金只是对以化学为主的一些神秘现象的研究的总称而已，并不是炼黄金啊。\n{恶徒：}想蒙我们，没门！今天你一定要交出钱来，不然……\n\n{伊娜：}住手，不带这么欺负人的。\n{恶徒：}嗯？你们又是谁？你们是这个死炼金术士的朋友吗？来替他交钱来了？\n{伊娜：}我刚才听到了，你们凭什么敲诈人家？\n{恶徒：}就凭我们是龙牙山好汉！\n{伊娜：}又是龙牙山好汉，一帮强盗。\n{恶徒：}竟敢说我们是强盗，你活得不耐烦了！弟兄们，先把这丫头收拾了，再去处理那个死炼金术士。\n\n\n\n"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA seal is affixed to a box.","一个箱子上贴着封条。"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA simple little room caught Ina's attention. This small room looks abrupt among the luxurious palace buildings, and it doesn't even have windows. The only door was locked.\n{Ina:} Look, this house is so strange. Could the \"Fire Spirit Orb\" be hidden here?\n{Freeman:} Break the lock and see. After the door was broken open, there was no treasure inside, only a haggard old man lying on a shabby bed. When the old man saw someone coming in, his expression turned into anger, and he yelled in a trembling voice.\n{Old man:} Stop giving me food! Tell me Horia, just kill me!\n{Ina:} What is this grandpa? Looks like Holia is locked here?\n{Old man:} Huh? You are not Hollia's men?\n{Freeman:} No. Excuse me, senior?\n{Old man:} Don't ask who I am. Let me go out, I want the old thief Holia to go desperately.\n{Freeman:} Senior, please don't be impulsive. Holia has been defeated by us.\n{Old man:} Really?\n{Ina:} Really, if you don't believe me, go out and watch.\n{Old man:} Okay, great, this old thief also has today. What reward do you want?\n{Freeman:} This, we are not here for rewards, but he repeatedly tried to harm us, and we were forced to act with him. He has another treasure, the \"Fire Spirit Orb\", which is very important to us, so we want to find it.\n{Old man:} It turned out to be like this. The treasure must be in the treasure room of the old thief. You come with me.","一间简陋的小房引起了伊娜的注意。这小房在豪华的宫殿建筑之间显得很突兀，而且连窗户都没有。唯一的门被上了锁。\n\n{伊娜：}看，这间房子好奇怪。“火灵珠”会不会就藏在这里面呢？\n{弗里曼：}把锁打破看看。\n\n门被破开后，里面并没有任何宝物，只有一张破旧的床上躺着一个憔悴的老头。老头看见有人进来，表情变成愤怒，用颤抖的声音嚷嚷起来。\n\n{老头：}不要再给我送食物了！你们给我告诉霍利亚，直接杀了我便罢！\n{伊娜：}请问这位爷爷是？看起来被霍利亚关在这里啊？\n{老头：}嗯？你们不是霍利亚的手下？\n{弗里曼：}不是。请问前辈是？\n{老头：}不要问我是谁。让我出去，我要找霍利亚那个老贼拼命去。\n{弗里曼：}前辈请不要冲动。霍利亚已经被我们打倒了。\n{老头：}真的吗？\n{伊娜：}真的耶，不信您出去看。\n{老头：}好，太好了，这老贼也有今天。你们要什么奖赏？\n{弗里曼：}这个，我们并不是为奖赏而来，只是他屡次想加害我们，我们被逼了才跟他动手的。另外有一件对我们很重要的宝物“火灵珠”被他据为己有了，所以我们想找到这件东西。\n{老头：}原来是这样。宝物肯定在那个老贼的藏宝室里。你们跟我来。\n\n"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA simple-dressed young man is playing with a telescope, and there are many other utensils and materials beside it. He didn't notice the approach of Ina and others at all.\n{Ina:} Hello, may I ask...\n{Youth:} Wow! It scared me to death, don't speak next to me suddenly.\n{Ina:} Uh, I'm sorry, I didn't expect you to be so focused...\n{Youth:} Having been unsure, my head is big...\n{Ina:} What are you doing?\n{Youth:} I'm working on an astronomical telescope. It is assembled according to the method in the book, but the observation effect is always not very good.\n{Freeman:} Is this a refracting telescope you use?\n{Youth:} Are there any other types of telescopes? I only introduced such a kind in this book.\n{Freeman:} Your book is a bit old, no wonder. Astronomical telescopes generally have two types: refracting telescopes and reflecting telescopes. The refracting telescopes have been known to everyone for a long time, and the reflecting telescopes were invented in recent years, and the effect is better than that of the refracting telescopes. There seems to be a record in the book I brought from the library.\n{Youth:} Really? Great, can you show me.\n{Freeman:} Is there any more material? Let's assemble another reflecting telescope together.\n{Youth:} Good, good.\n{Ina:} Uh...Jack, you're so excited...\n{Freeman:} Don't worry, you'll be fine soon.\n{Rael:} Then I will help too.\n{Ina:} Okay, okay, I'll come too.\n{Youth:} It turns out that the telescope can still do this. I didn't expect it... After a few hours...\n{Freeman:} It's done.\n{Youth:} Awesome! Let me take a look. Let me take a look... It really is much better than the previous one. Haha! I am so happy today. Then this extra refracting telescope will be given to you, as a thank you for helping me. But what did you guys find me about before?\n{Ina:} Uh, it's not easy, finally back to the topic... We are actually just trying to ask a way. We want to go to {Eldria}, I wonder if we are going here? There seems to be no way...\n{Youth:} Eldria is not far from here, yes, but he can't get there from here. I don't know exactly how to go.\n{Ina:} Okay, then let's find a way by ourselves...\n{Youth:} There is the base of the \"Red Sea Fleet\" of Solo's men. Those guys are not reasonable, you'd better not provoke them.\n{Ina:} Really, thanks for the advice...","一个衣着简朴的青年正在摆弄着一架望远镜，旁边还有不少其他器具和材料。对伊娜等人的靠近全然没有察觉。\n\n{伊娜：}你好，请问……\n{青年：}哇！吓死我了，不要突然在我旁边说话。\n{伊娜：}呃，对不起，没想到你这么专注……\n{青年：}一直搞不定啊，头都大了……\n{伊娜：}你在做什么呢？\n{青年：}我在弄天文望远镜。按照书上的方法组装好了，不过观测效果总是不太好。\n{弗里曼：}你用的这是折射望远镜吧？\n{青年：}望远镜还有种类吗？我这本书上只介绍了这么一种啊。\n{弗里曼：}你这本书有点旧，也难怪。天文望远镜一般有折射望远镜和反射望远镜两种，折射望远镜早就被大家所知了，而反射望远镜是近些年才发明出来的，效果比折射望远镜好。我从图书馆里带来的书上好像有记载。\n{青年：}是吗？太好了，能不能给我看看。\n{弗里曼：}还有材料吗？我们一起来再组装个反射望远镜吧。\n{青年：}好啊好啊。\n{伊娜：}呃……杰克，你来劲了啊……\n{弗里曼：}不用担心，很快就好。\n{雷尔：}那么我也来帮忙吧。\n{伊娜：}好吧好吧，我也来。\n{青年：}原来望远镜还可以这样做啊，真没想到……\n\n几个小时之后……\n\n{弗里曼：}搞定了。\n{青年：}真棒！我来看看我来看看……果然比之前那个好多了。哈哈！今天真是太开心了。那么这个多余的折射望远镜，就送给你们吧，算是对你们帮助我的答谢。不过，你们之前找我是有什么事呢？\n{伊娜：}呃，不容易，终于回到主题了……我们其实只是想借问个路。我们想去{埃尔德里亚}，不知是不是往这里走啊？好像没有路了……\n{青年：}埃尔德里亚是在这里附近不远没错，不过，从这里到达不了。到底该怎么走其实我也不清楚。\n{伊娜：}好吧，那么我们自己想办法……\n{青年：}那里是索罗的手下“赤海舰队”的根据地，那帮家伙可不讲理了，你们最好别去招惹他们。\n{伊娜：}是吗，谢谢忠告……\n\n\n\n"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA small church is located at the foot of the mountain. A priest was praying in front of the idol.\n{Priest:} Augustine, God of Glory, please restore peace to the land of the Barland Kingdom...\n{Ina:}... {Priest:} What are you looking at at the door, I heard you come in.\n{Ina:} I'm sorry...\n{Priest:} If you want to pray too, then you have come to the wrong place. Only Augustine, the god of glory, is enshrined here.\n{Ina:} Is there anything wrong?\n{Priest:} Looks like you are not a local? Here, due to the religious policy of the Barland Kingdom, Augustine's followers were ostracized and very few remained. Most people did not realize the light of the gods, but succumbed to the authority of the king. ?a?aAlso, those vulgar people change their beliefs for a little benefit, and they are not worthy to pray before the glorious god Augustine. Their belief in the gods is not a true reverence for the gods, but just trying to bribe the gods for personal gain. I still don't want the solemn hall to be trampled on by those people.\n{Ina:} Although the reason is like this, isn't it a bit too harsh to say that...\n{Priest:} Isn't it? Those who pray for wealth, children, and promotion are just this class. I don't want to work with my own hands and hope to get benefits by bribing the gods. This is simply an insult to the gods. The gods are kind, compassionate, but also just. They will never satisfy their selfish desires because of the incense given by individual people. The gods are not so corrupt.\n{Ina:} Our village generally prays for good weather and rain...\n{Priest:} Well, this is true piety. First of all, this is not for self-interest but for everyone. Second, even if the weather is smooth, you still need your own labor to get the harvest. Such simple people are believers admired by the gods. However, this alone is not enough. To pray here, you must be a person accepted by the gods, and you also need a higher state of mind. Well, let me see if you really came here under the guidance of a god.","一间并不宽敞的教堂座落在山脚下。一个神官正在神像前祷告。\n\n{神官：}光辉之神奥古斯丁，请让巴兰德王国这片土地恢复宁静……\n{伊娜：}……\n{神官：}你在门口看什么呢，我听到你进来了。\n{伊娜：}对不起……\n{神官：}如果你也是想要祷告，那么你是来错地方了。这里只供奉光辉之神奥古斯丁。\n{伊娜：}有什么不对吗？\n{神官：}看起来你不是本地人？这里由于巴兰德王国的宗教政策，奥古斯丁的信徒遭到排斥，已经所剩无几。大多数人并没有领悟到神明的光芒，而是屈服于国王的权威。——也罢，那些低俗的人为了一点利益而改变信仰，他们也不配在光辉之神奥古斯丁前面祷告。他们信仰神明并非是真正的对神明崇敬，而只是试图贿赂神明以取得私利而已。我还不希望庄严的殿堂被那些人踩踏呢。\n{伊娜：}虽然道理是这样，不过这么说是不是有点太苛刻了……\n{神官：}难道不是吗？那些祈求发财的，祈求生子的，祈求升官的，都不过是这等人而已。不想通过自己的双手劳动，指望通过贿赂神明来获得利益，这简直是对神明的侮辱。神明是善良，慈悲的，但又是公正的，他们绝不会因为个别人给的香火更多就去满足他们的私欲，神明没这么腐败。\n{伊娜：}我们村里一般都是祈求风调雨顺之类的啦……\n{神官：}嗯，这才是真正的虔诚。首先这并非是为自己的私利而是为了大家，其次，即使风调雨顺，也仍然需要自己的劳动才能获得收成。这样朴实的人们才是神明所欣赏的信徒。不过，光是这样还不够。在我这里祷告，必须是神明所接受的人，还需要更高的心境。好吧，让我看看，你是否真的是由神明的引导而来到这里。\n\n\n\n"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA small team of demons chased towards Ina, but it didn't take long for Ina to be far behind.\n{Ina:} You want to catch up with me here a hundred years ago. Although I really want to beat you up, I'm really sorry, now my primary goal is not you, and it won't be too late to clean up you after I take Slander away.","有一小支魔族的队伍朝伊娜这边追来，不过没多久就被伊娜远远地甩在后面。\n{伊娜：}想在这里追上我，你们还早一百年呢。虽然我也很想揍你们一顿，不过实在抱歉，现在我的首要目标不是你们，等我收抬掉斯兰德，再清理你们不迟。"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA steaming hole in the ground.","冒热气的地洞。"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA tall stone tablet is engraved with densely packed words, which are all praises and praises to the deeds of Culled VII during his lifetime.\n{Ina:} Bah! A tyrant, still writes so high-sounding.","一块高大的石碑上刻着密密麻麻的文字，都是对库里德七世生前事迹的歌颂和赞美。\n{伊娜：}呸！一个暴君，还写得这么冠冕堂皇。"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA team of people rushed up in front of her in a panic. Ina was planning to hide, but she saw that one of the team was Rael. The others are all dressed up by local indigenous people, and one of them, the short white beard holding a rod of animal teeth, looks to be their leader.\n{Ina:} Rael! finally I find you.\n{Rael:} Ah, is it Ina? Did you come in as expected? Broken...\n{Ina:} Broken?\n{Elder:} The barrier must have been destroyed by them with the \"Fire Spirit Orb\".\n{Rael:} Sorry, elder, it's all my fault. Is there any remedy now?\n{Elder:} No more.\n{Rael:} Ina, when you came in, was there no one to stop you? The elder left someone there to inform you.\n{Ina:} Oh, so, when we came in, we saw a corpse, dressed similarly to those of them... Could it be that...\n{Rael:} The person notified was killed by someone else, no wonder...\n{ Elder:} Besides them, anyone else knows the entrance?\n{Freeman:} If there is, it must be the demons.\n{Rael:} I miscalculated, I was too impatient. It would be great if I stayed there.\n{Ina:} What the hell is going on? I know I got into trouble, but can you tell us everything from beginning to end, maybe...maybe we still have a way...","前面慌慌张张跑来一队人，伊娜正打算隐蔽，却看到队中一人正是雷尔。而其他人则都是当地土著的打扮，其中一个攥着兽牙杖的白胡子矮个看起来是他们的头儿。\n\n{伊娜：}雷尔！终于找到你了。\n{雷尔：}啊，是伊娜？果然是你进来了吗？坏了……\n{伊娜：}坏了？\n{长老：}结界肯定是被他们用“火灵珠”破坏了。\n{雷尔：}对不起，长老，都是我的错。现在还有什么补救办法吗？\n{长老：}没有了。\n{雷尔：}伊娜，你们进来的时候，没有谁阻止你们吗？长老留了一个人在那里通知你们的。\n{伊娜：}啊，这么说来，我们进来时，看到一个尸体，穿着跟他们这些人差不多……难道说……\n{雷尔：}通知的人被其他人干掉了，难怪……\n{长老：}除了他们，还有别的人知道那个入口？\n{弗里曼：}如果有的话，一定就是魔族了。\n{雷尔：}我失算了，我太心急了。如果当时我留在那里就好了。\n{伊娜：}到底是怎么回事？我知道我闯祸了，不过能不能把事情从头到尾告诉我们，也许……也许我们还有办法……"},
 {"ira-the-mage-3\nA woman wearing a robe of a mage appeared in front of them.\n{Woman:} Don't you think it's a bit rude to break into here without authorization? Just like the little prince who sneaked in two years ago...\n{Ina:} Ah, I'm sorry, we just wanted to ask Senior Mengying for some questions.\n{Woman:} I am Mengying.\n{Ina:} Huh? I thought that the so-called hermit with supernatural powers must be an old white-bearded grandfather, but I didn't expect it to be an aunt...\n{Mengying:} presumptuous! I want to call my sister!\n{Ina:} I'm sorry, sorry, sister Mengying. I'm wrong. I apologize. And we broke in privately to cause you trouble.\n{Rael:} I broke in because of my business, and I should apologize. Apologize to the predecessors.\n{Mengying:} Forget it, since you can get in here, it seems that you still have some ability. Tell me what you want to ask.\n{Ina:} Ah, thank you sister Mengying! We are looking for something called \"Dragon King Divine Power\" and want to know where it is.\n{Mengying:} What? Are you looking for Dragon King's supernatural power? I advise you to give up this idea.\n{Rael:} Why? It is very important to me.\n{Mengying:} If you are going to find it, you will encounter unimaginable dangers, and you may not be able to come back alive. It is important to you, is it more important than life?\n{Rael:} Yes, it is more important than life. My hometown of Ariania was occupied by the demons. Only the power of the Dragon King can help me drive away the demons and restore my country. It is for this that I came here, otherwise I would have chosen to fight to death with my comrades.\n{Mengying:} What, Aryania fell into the hands of the demons? Okay, then I decided to help you guys.\n{Rael:} Thank you very much, senior.","一个穿着法师长袍的女子出现在两人面前。\n{女子：}你们两个擅自闯进这里，不觉得有点失礼吗？就跟两年前不怕死活溜进来的那个小王子一样……\n{伊娜：}啊，对不起，我们只是想来找梦影前辈请教点问题。\n{女子：}我就是梦影。\n{伊娜：}啊？我还以为所谓的神通广大的隐士，一定是个白胡子老爷爷呢，没想到是个阿姨……\n{梦影：}放肆！要叫姐姐！\n{伊娜：}对不起对不起，梦影姐姐。我错了。我道歉。还有我们私自闯进来给您添麻烦了。\n{雷尔：}是因为我的事情才闯进来的，该道歉的是我。向前辈赔罪。\n{梦影：}算啦，既然你们能进得到这里，看来还是有点本事的。告诉我你们想问什么吧。\n{伊娜：}啊，谢谢梦影姐姐！我们在找一件叫“龙王神力”的东西，想知道它在哪里。\n{梦影：}什么？你们要找龙王神力？我劝你们放弃这个想法比较好。\n{雷尔：}为什么？它对我很重要。\n{梦影：}如果你要去找，你会遇到难以想像的危险，你可能没法活着回来。它对你很重要，难道比生命还重要？\n{雷尔：}对，确实比生命还重要。我的故乡亚利安尼亚被魔族占领了，只有龙王神力能帮助我赶走魔族光复我的国家。就是为了这个我才来到这里，否则我早就选择与战友一起战死沙场了。\n{梦影：}什么，亚利安尼亚落入了魔族手中？好吧，那么我决定帮你们了。\n{雷尔：}十分感谢前辈。"},
